# What an install of claude-fleet holds — the ONE list (claude-fleet#2771,
# EPIC #2770 C1). The hub filters each stable's tree by the copy inside that
# commit (tokenledger internal/release TreeList), and
# bin/release-tree-selftest.sh reds when a script in bin/ reads a top-level
# item of the repo that this list leaves out.
#
#   dir/    every file under it        !dir/   never anything under it
#   path    that one file              !path   never that file
#   *       every top-level file not starting with "."
#
# A `!` wins over `dir/` and `*`; an exact `path` wins over a `!dir/`.

# the runtime trees
bin/
conf/
agents/
hooks/
commands/
skills/
mod/
shell/
launchd/
systemd/
docs/

# read by a login's install too: the plugin manifest (fleet-lib.sh,
# fleet-install-apply.sh) and the laptop / proxy halves (fleet-doctor.sh,
# open-url.sh)
.claude-plugin/
extras/

# README.md, LICENSE, release.json, fleet.conf.example, …
*

# never: the hub's Go source, its deploy tree, the CI's files
!tokenledger/
!deploy/
!.github/
